# Songkhla–Pattani Coastal Shoreline Analysis (DSAS WebGIS)
excerpt: "<br/><img src='/images/adsas1.png'>"
excerpt: "<br/><img src='/images/adsas2.png'>"
An interactive Streamlit WebGIS application for analyzing coastal erosion and accretion along the Songkhla–Pattani coastline and Laem Tachi Spit using multi-year Landsat satellite imagery (1984–2026).

🚀 [Launch Live App](https://songkhla-pattani-dsas.streamlit.app/) | 💻 [View Source Code (`app.py`)](https://github.com/aleena-cha/aleena-cha.github.io/blob/master/_layouts/dsas/app.py)**

---

### Key Capabilities
Automated Shoreline Extraction: Extracts annual shorelines using MNDWI and K-Means Iso Cluster classification.
DSAS Metric Computation: Generates an onshore baseline from the earliest selected year and casts perpendicular transects to compute SCE, NSM, EPR, and LRR.
Interactive Exploration: Allows users to customize analysis parameters and inspect results directly on an interactive Folium satellite map.
Publication-Ready Exports: Export 300 DPI maps, profile graphs, CSV tables, and GeoJSON layers for further GIS analysis.
